A||||3||Hairy_Fiero||84Se brake problems||||5||
Z||000000||Hairy_Fiero||12-15-2001||09:47 PM||||Have an 84Se 4banger with stock brakes and rotors. Replaced the pads, rotors are well within spec so I re-used them. Bled the brake system. Worked fine after that for about 800 miles then I let the car sit. Now the brake pedal travels all the way to the floor, and barely stops the car. Fluid level is fine, nothing visually wrong with any of the brakes. Not sure where to start any help much appreciated.<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||12-16-2001||12:02 AM||||Depending on how long you let the car sit (and where), it could have some condensation in the brake fluid now.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-16-2001||11:32 AM||||Is the fluid in your master cylinder low?  If not it is probably a bad master cylinder or you need to rebleed the brakes.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-16-2001||04:43 PM||||Most likely the MC was on it's way to dead. Just picked now to do it.<P>replace the MC and flush new fluid thru the system.<P>read the service and fluid articles in my cave.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
